---
import BaseLayout from '../../layouts/BaseLayout.astro';
import { withBase } from '../../lib/paths';

const canonical = new URL(withBase('/work/yhct'), Astro.site).href;
const jsonLd = [
  {
    '@type': 'Article',
    '@id': `${canonical}#case-study`,
    headline: 'YHCT Clinical AI Platform — bounded agentic clinical AI',
    description: 'Case study of a clinician-facing AI platform with an interleaved agent loop, governed local corpus, clinical tools, provider portability, durable state, and explicit validation boundaries.',
    dateModified: '2026-08-25T10:30:00+07:00',
    author: { '@type': 'Person', name: 'Sang Truong', url: new URL(withBase('/about'), Astro.site).href },
    mainEntityOfPage: canonical,
    about: ['Clinical AI', 'AI agents', 'RAG', 'FastAPI', 'Next.js', 'PostgreSQL', 'Qdrant', 'MLOps'],
  },
  {
    '@type': 'BreadcrumbList',
    itemListElement: [
      { '@type': 'ListItem', position: 1, name: 'Home', item: new URL(withBase('/'), Astro.site).href },
      { '@type': 'ListItem', position: 2, name: 'YHCT Clinical AI Platform', item: canonical },
    ],
  },
];
---
<BaseLayout
  title="YHCT Clinical AI Platform — Agentic Clinical AI Case Study | Sang Truong"
  description="Deep technical case study: bounded agentic clinical AI, governed offline corpus research, clinical tool authority, OpenAI/local portability, durable conversation state, and self-hosted UAT validation."
  image="og-yhct.png"
  pageType="article"
  jsonLd={jsonLd}
>
  <article class="case container section">
    <a class="back-link" href={withBase('#work')}>← Selected work</a>
    <header class="case-hero">
      <p class="eyebrow">Case Study 01 · Clinical AI · 2026</p>
      <h1>YHCT Clinical AI Platform</h1>
      <p class="case-lede">A clinician-facing AI assistant designed so model flexibility and clinical authority can coexist without pretending they are the same thing.</p>
      <div class="case-meta">
        <div><span>Role</span><strong>AI Architect / Lead Builder</strong></div>
        <div><span>Runtime</span><strong>Agent · tools · local corpus · durable state</strong></div>
        <div><span>Stage</span><strong>Deployed UAT · clinician acceptance pending</strong></div>
      </div>
      <p class="case-verified">Last verified against current project state: <time datetime="2026-08-25">25 Aug 2026</time></p>
    </header>

    <section class="evidence-band" aria-label="Recorded validation evidence">
      <div><strong>855</strong><span>backend tests passed</span></div>
      <div><strong>301</strong><span>source files under strict mypy</span></div>
      <div><strong>30</strong><span>frontend rendering contracts passed</span></div>
      <div><strong>Self-hosted UAT</strong><span>runtime + browser validation recorded</span></div>
    </section>

    <section class="case-section visual-panel clinical-runtime" aria-label="YHCT agent runtime architecture">
      <div class="runtime-flow">
        <div class="runtime-node"><small>INPUT</small><strong>Clinician + files + conversation</strong></div>
        <span class="runtime-arrow">→</span>
        <div class="runtime-node runtime-node-hot"><small>MAIN AGENT</small><strong>FINAL · CALL_TOOLS · ASK_USER</strong></div>
        <span class="runtime-arrow">→</span>
        <div class="runtime-tools">
          <span>Clinical tools</span><span>Local corpus research</span><span>Files + compute</span>
        </div>
        <span class="runtime-arrow runtime-return">↺</span>
        <div class="runtime-node"><small>OUTPUT</small><strong>Grounded answer + durable state</strong></div>
      </div>
    </section>

    <section class="case-section case-grid">
      <div><p class="eyebrow">Problem</p><h2>Clinical AI cannot rely on fluent answers alone.</h2></div>
      <div class="case-copy">
        <p>A useful clinician assistant has to accept natural language, prescriptions, tables, and documents while keeping track of what it actually knows, which source or tool owns each fact, what conversation state should persist, and what happens when evidence is missing.</p>
        <p>The hard problem was not “add an LLM to a hospital UI.” It was designing the boundary between flexible model reasoning and governed clinical facts so the system can remain useful without silently upgrading model prose into clinical authority.</p>
      </div>
    </section>

    <section class="case-section section-rule case-grid">
      <div><p class="eyebrow">My ownership</p><h2>Architecture through acceptance.</h2></div>
      <div class="ownership-list">
        <article><strong>AI/runtime architecture</strong><p>Defined the bounded interleaved agent loop, action contract, tool scheduling boundaries, context controls, and provider-neutral model port.</p></article>
        <article><strong>Clinical authority model</strong><p>Separated model synthesis from authoritative tool/source facts so interaction severity, source identity, and structured findings cannot be silently rewritten by prose.</p></article>
        <article><strong>Knowledge and retrieval</strong><p>Designed local-corpus acquisition, hybrid retrieval/reranking, source navigation, provenance, and the runtime ban on arbitrary live web fetches.</p></article>
        <article><strong>Product and deployment</strong><p>Owned the clinician chat shape, durable state, file flows, environment profiles, evaluation gates, self-hosted execution checks, and handoff boundaries.</p></article>
      </div>
    </section>

    <section class="case-section section-rule">
      <p class="eyebrow">Core runtime contract</p>
      <div class="contract-grid">
        <div class="code-card"><span class="code-comment">// one validated action each model round</span><strong>FINAL | CALL_TOOLS | ASK_USER</strong><span class="code-comment">// bounded rounds, tool calls, concurrency, and wall time</span></div>
        <div class="principle-card"><span>MODEL</span><strong>owns workflow + answer synthesis</strong><span>TOOLS / SOURCES</span><strong>own the facts they return</strong></div>
      </div>
    </section>

    <section class="case-section section-rule">
      <p class="eyebrow">Architecture decisions</p>
      <div class="decision-grid decision-grid-3">
        <article><span>01</span><h3>Bounded agent loop</h3><p>The model can choose to answer, call tools, or ask for missing information, but total rounds, tool calls, concurrency, repeat calls, and turn wall time are bounded.</p></article>
        <article><span>02</span><h3>Explicit fact ownership</h3><p>Clinical tools and retrieved sources own the facts they return. Assistant prose remains context, not clinical authority.</p></article>
        <article><span>03</span><h3>Offline corpus at runtime</h3><p>Public and hospital-approved sources are acquired ahead of time; clinician turns search the governed local corpus instead of arbitrary live URLs.</p></article>
        <article><span>04</span><h3>Provider portability</h3><p>The same application-level action contract can run through OpenAI or a fully local OpenAI-compatible model path without silent cloud fallback.</p></article>
        <article><span>05</span><h3>Resumable state</h3><p>Recent messages, rolling summaries, active clinical items, prior observations, attachments, and clarification checkpoints are kept durable and bounded.</p></article>
        <article><span>06</span><h3>Pragmatic platform shape</h3><p>FastAPI + Next.js + PostgreSQL, with Qdrant, MinIO/S3, and Redis where they serve a concrete runtime boundary rather than architecture fashion.</p></article>
      </div>
    </section>

    <section class="case-section section-rule case-grid">
      <div><p class="eyebrow">Executable scope</p><h2>What the current UAT candidate actually supports.</h2></div>
      <div class="capability-grid">
        <article><h3>Clinical tools</h3><p>Drug/herb interaction checks, drug/herb lookup, prescription review.</p></article>
        <article><h3>Corpus research</h3><p>Search corpus, open results, search within a source, and reformulate across bounded model rounds.</p></article>
        <article><h3>Documents</h3><p>TXT, Markdown, text-extractable PDF, DOCX, CSV, XLS, XLSX, plus bounded attachment navigation.</p></article>
        <article><h3>State & UI</h3><p>Protected clinician chat, conversation history, multi-file composer, SSE progress, evidence/source details, and role-gated data/knowledge administration.</p></article>
      </div>
    </section>

    <section class="case-section section-rule case-grid">
      <div><p class="eyebrow">Deliberate non-claims</p><h2>Scope is part of reliability.</h2></div>
      <div class="case-copy">
        <p>The current candidate does <strong>not</strong> claim image vision, scanned-document OCR, audio/video input, live web freshness, provider-native token streaming, exhaustive black-box clinical evaluation, production deployment, or production acceptance.</p>
        <p>Those boundaries matter because “source implemented,” “runtime validated,” “clinician tested,” and “production accepted” are different evidence levels.</p>
      </div>
    </section>

    <section class="case-section section-rule">
      <p class="eyebrow">Recorded validation state · 2026-08-25</p>
      <div class="status-table" role="table" aria-label="YHCT validation status">
        <div role="row"><span role="cell">Source implementation</span><strong role="cell" class="status-ok">Validated candidate</strong></div>
        <div role="row"><span role="cell">Backend / type / frontend build gates</span><strong role="cell" class="status-ok">Passed</strong></div>
        <div role="row"><span role="cell">Self-hosted UAT execution</span><strong role="cell" class="status-ok">Passed</strong></div>
        <div role="row"><span role="cell">Automated desktop/mobile browser matrix</span><strong role="cell" class="status-ok">Passed</strong></div>
        <div role="row"><span role="cell">Manual clinician acceptance / hospital handoff</span><strong role="cell" class="status-wip">Pending</strong></div>
        <div role="row"><span role="cell">Production deployment / production acceptance</span><strong role="cell">Not claimed</strong></div>
      </div>
    </section>

    <section class="case-section demo-placeholder">
      <div>
        <p class="eyebrow">Public demo boundary</p>
        <h2>Sanitized proof, never hospital production.</h2>
        <p>A future public demo should use synthetic prescriptions, sanitized knowledge, isolated credentials, no patient data, no production hospital integration, no admin surface, and explicit rate limits. The production/UAT system itself is not the portfolio demo.</p>
      </div>
      <span class="status-pill">Demo not public yet</span>
    </section>
  </article>
</BaseLayout>
